{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#339","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#339","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#339\",\"parent_revision\":\"8f099525dc2c90738ee14751a0840d6671232b46\",\"root_revision\":\"fc32e75b45122506d8505a909ed087e95d67cbd169e5d98de4798796e5a02907\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDuring #338 implementation, the orchestrator found Task 1.1 still IN PROGRESS after the sub-agent completed. Instead of investigating why the SubagentStop hook didn't update the status (checking hook logs, active-task context file, hook script expectations), the orchestrator directly edited the task plan file with a guessed timestamp. This violates: (1) orchestrator must not edit implementation files, (2) status updates go through task_status_hook.py, (3) unexpected behavior requires investigation not workaround. The flawed reasoning was 'the agent was spawned via Agent tool, not via the Skill tool with start-task' \u2014 but skills don't spawn agents; the Skill() call inside the Agent loads instructions, the hook fires on AgentStop regardless. Root cause of the hook not updating status needs investigation.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **orchestrator manually edited task status instead of investigating hook failure** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: session observation during #338 implementation\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-15)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n\\nFunctional intent: PRESENT \u2014 orchestrator bypassed SubagentStop hook and directly edited plan file with guessed timestamp.\\n\\nScope boundaries: PRESENT \u2014 in-scope is why hook failed and how to prevent recurrence. Out-of-scope: broader SAM pipeline.\\n\\nExternal interfaces: PRESENT \u2014 hooks.json SubagentStop entry, task_status_hook.py, active-task context file, agent_transcript_path in hook input.\\n\\nExisting system context: PRESENT \u2014 hook script, hooks.json, start-task skill all verified in codebase.\\n\\nConstraints: PARTIAL \u2014 root cause unconfirmed. Whether Agent-tool spawn vs Skill-call spawn affects hook firing is not yet tested.\\n\\nVerification expectations: PARTIAL \u2014 no reproduction steps from session #338 were captured.\\n\\nMissing inputs: root cause of hook non-firing; session context from #338; exact prompt passed to sub-agent.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nThe failure was observed during session #338 but no reproduction steps were recorded. A reproduction requires:\\n\\n1. Start a task via `/dh:start-task <plan-file> --task <task-id>` so that `active-task-{session_id}.json` is written to `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/`.\\n2. Spawn a sub-agent via the `Agent` tool (not via an inline `Skill()` call \u2014 per the item's reported spawn method).\\n3. Wait for the sub-agent to complete (triggering SubagentStop).\\n4. Inspect the task plan file: check whether `status: complete` and `completed: <timestamp>` were written.\\n5. Check hook stderr for any `[hook] SubagentStop:` messages \u2014 look for \\\"no agent_transcript_path\\\", \\\"could not extract session_id\\\", or silent exit-0 paths.\\n\\nThe silent skip paths in `task_status_hook.py` are at lines 712, 720, 806\u2013807, 811\u2013815, 819\u2013822, 829\u2013831.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\nTask 1.1 remained status in-progress after sub-agent completion (observed in session #338). No hook stderr output was captured \u2014 the hook exited 0 silently. The manually written timestamp does not match actual completion time. Diagnostic: run sam status on the plan after sub-agent completion to see stale in-progress state.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n6/10 \u2014 Direct harm is a data integrity violation (incorrect timestamps, manual edit bypassing the SAM write path). Systemic harm is the orchestrator flawed reasoning was not refuted. P1 classification is correct.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nBlocks reliable automatic task completion tracking for all SAM workflows. Any session where sub-agents complete tasks started via Agent tool risks the same silent skip and stale status. Affects task_status_hook.py, hooks.json SubagentStop entry, start-task skill, and the active-task context file mechanism.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\nConfirms or refutes whether SubagentStop fires when sub-agents are spawned via Agent tool vs Skill() call \u2014 closing an undocumented assumption in the hook system. Establishes a reproduction test that can catch future hook regressions. Prevents the orchestrator workaround pattern from recurring via a code fix or documentation guard. Correct timestamps in task plans enable accurate audit trails for feature completion.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a sub-agent completes work that was started with /dh:start-task (which writes active-task-{session_id}.json), the SubagentStop hook fires automatically, reads the context file via the sub-agent's session ID, updates the task plan file to status complete with a completed timestamp via sam_update_status, and clears the context file. The orchestrator does not edit the plan file \u2014 it reads the updated status via the SAM MCP tool after the hook completes.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n1. Root cause of the hook non-firing in session #338 is identified with a falsifiable test \u2014 not assumed from the spawn method.\\n2. A reproduction command exists demonstrating the hook fires or fails to fire under the specific spawn conditions observed in #338.\\n3. If the hook does not fire when sub-agents are spawned via Agent tool: the condition is fixed or explicitly documented as a known limitation in start-task/SKILL.md.\\n4. If the hook fires correctly under all spawn paths: the orchestrator's flawed reasoning is captured as an anti-pattern in the orchestrator-discipline rules.\\n5. No plan files contain timestamps written outside sam_update_status in task_status_hook.py.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. A reproduction test demonstrates the exact conditions (spawn method, context file state, hook input fields present or absent) under which the SubagentStop hook fires vs silently exits.\\n2. The root cause statement is supported by evidence from the hook script execution path \u2014 not inferred from the spawn method alone.\\n3. If the hook fails to fire under Agent-tool spawns: a fix is implemented and the reproduction test passes after the fix.\\n4. If the hook fires correctly under all spawn methods: the orchestrator's mistaken reasoning is documented as an anti-pattern in plugins/orchestrator-discipline/rules/CLAUDE.md or start-task/SKILL.md.\\n5. Running task_status_hook.py with a simulated SubagentStop JSON payload (containing a valid agent_transcript_path whose session ID maps to a real active-task file) sets status complete in the target task file.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\nHook script: plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py\\nHook config: plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json (SubagentStop entry lines 70-79)\\nStart-task skill: plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md\\nWorkflow docs: plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md (Section 6.1 SubagentStop)\\nOrchestrator rules: plugins/orchestrator-discipline/rules/CLAUDE.md\\nFix-delegation rule: .claude/rules/fix-delegation-discipline.md\\nSkill: /find-cause\\nSkill: /dh:start-task\\nRelated bug: #408 \u2014 Implementation Manager lacks DEFERRED/SKIPPED status (same task-status system)\\nRelated feature: #257 \u2014 Task Status MCP wrapping\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nDepends on: None \u2014 investigation can start immediately from the hook script source and existing documentation.\\nBlocks: #408 (DEFERRED/SKIPPED status) is an adjacent bug in the same task-status system; investigation findings may inform that item's fix scope.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNo hook stderr output from session #338 was captured; the reproduction must be constructed from the item description and hook script source.\\n\\nThe exact prompt text passed to the sub-agent in #338 is unknown \u2014 this affects whether the prompt-parsing fallback path (hook lines 371-374) would have matched.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall/Medium \u2014 Investigation and root cause identification is Small (hook script is well-documented with enumerable failure paths at lines 712, 720, 806-807, 811-815, 819-822, 829-831). A code fix is Medium only if the hook genuinely fails to fire under Agent-tool spawns. If the hook fires correctly and the issue is orchestrator reasoning, the fix is documentation-only (Small).\\n\",\"digest\":\"375732204473163335e8d3f9cda72741b16c0d8ca520a9fe7b3af15839644674\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnNNmg\"}"}